# TypeScript/JavaScript Coding Style

## Immutability

Never mutate objects in place. Always return new copies:

```typescript
// BAD: Mutation
function updateMetric(metric, value) {
  metric.value = value  // mutates original
  return metric
}

// GOOD: Immutability
function updateMetric(metric, value) {
  return { ...metric, value }
}
```

## Error Handling

Use async/await with try-catch. Never swallow errors silently:

```typescript
// BAD
try {
  await riskyOperation()
} catch (e) {}

// GOOD
try {
  const result = await riskyOperation()
  return result
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Operation failed:', error)
  throw new Error('User-facing message with context')
}
```

## Input Validation

Use Zod at all system boundaries — API responses, file uploads, external data:

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod'

const TrackMetricSchema = z.object({
  value: z.number(),
  unit: z.string(),
  qualityLevel: z.enum(['high', 'caution', 'invalid']),
  coverageRatio: z.number().min(0).max(1)
})

const validated = TrackMetricSchema.parse(externalData)
```

## Console.log

No `console.log` in production code. Use structured logging or remove before committing.

## File Size

Functions under 50 lines. Files under 800 lines. Extract when either limit approaches.
